> I have multiple distributions that could describe some data, and I want to construct a weighted mixed distribution. The weights across the mixed distribution should be based on their success at describing data seen so far, in a Bayesian fashion. Is there a conjugate prior for the weights of a mixed distribution, like I'm describing?
